Preserved safety state
----------------------
The evidence phase remains daemon-reloaded. The candidate is
loaded/inactive/dead/static, Restart=no, RuntimeMaxUSec=3min, NRestarts=0,
with zero start timestamps, zero journal lines and no runtime status or lock.
No Unit, manifest, Control-link or candidate action followed the failure.

Versioned correction
--------------------
All direct release-gate invocations set PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1. A dedicated
recover-bytecode-resume mode accepts only the exact daemon-reloaded phase,
the two exact bytecode paths/hashes and otherwise clean release. It moves the
entire __pycache__ directory to root-private M4.25 evidence, changes no tracked
file, proves the release clean, then runs the full stopped post-verification.
No file is deleted and rollback is not automatic.

Rollback plan
-------------
If the recovery boundary differs or post-verification still fails, stop and
preserve both release and evidence. The existing separately callable rollback
mode can restore old Unit, manifest and Control link only while the candidate
remains never started.
